ready to test the new 2.4.1 kernel.  Since I'm totally unfamilliar with
SRM, and still learning i'd thought I'd ask the list if there are any
gotchas I should be on the look out for when installing a new kernel.  Way
back (last week) in Milo days I just recompiled the kernel and added a new
boot section to the alphabios.  That way I could boot the new kernel, but
could also go back very easily if there was a problem.

Whats the best way to do this in SRM?  I currently have my SRM set up so
all I have to do is type boot.  Any one else had any upgrade expereince
with 2.4.1?


