Hi,

I may have to replace OpenVMS with Linux since Oracle has not released
Portal (WebDB) for their 8i product line yet, and perhaps they won't. I'm
not very happy to replace OpenVMS with Unix for some reasons, but I was
reading that Linux on Alpha is not a bad thing.

I would like to ask the following questions:

- can someone recommend or not recommend Linux on Alpha?

The server is a DS20 500 MHz, 640 MB RAM, single processor, 2 KZPCM-DX(DA)
(ultra scsi/fast Ethernet) combo cards, PowerStorm 4D10T graphics card.

- Is the above hardware well supported and functions reliable under Linux?
- is disk shadowing software available for Linux?

I also have an older DEC3000 server with Turbochannel, which I think might
be difficult to install a fully functional Linux on, any experiences?

Thanks!

