S.D. Brown wrote in <39D28419.CBAF5F06@cis.rit.edu>:
> 
> For example, mpg123(1) says the following when trying an MP3:
> > Playing MPEG stream from 03-What_Else_Is_New.mp3 ...
> > MPEG 1.0 layer III, 192 kbit/s, 44100 Hz stereo
> > mpg123: Can't rewind stream by 23 bits!
> > mpg123: Can't rewind stream by 13 bits!
> > mpg123: Can't rewind stream by 10 bits!
> > mpg123: Can't rewind stream by 21 bits!
> > mpg123: Can't rewind stream by 36 bits!
> > [until termination]

This is a problem in mpg123.  The fix can be found in the archives:
http://www.lib.uaa.alaska.edu/axp-list/archive/2000-10/0141.html

Find the attachment link at the bottom.  It's easy to patch by
hand in layer3.c in the mpg123 source, or in xmms, as it uses
the same file.  Recompile, and problem fixed.

Sorry I can't help with the rest.

