On Tue, Feb 27, 2001 at 12:01:52PM +0100, Christian Iseli wrote:
> 
> Just been trying out the latest kernel plus ac patches (2.4.2-ac5) on my
> LX164 alpha box.  All seems fine, except X :-(

Is this the first 2.4.x kernel you've tried, or just the first one that
shows this problem?

> Anybody seen this, and could tell me what's broken ?

Yes, I've just seen something like this.

Could you do an "lspci -v" and post the output?

> Do I need to recompile latest XFree ?  Or is it a kernel glitch ?

It's a conflict between kernel PCI resource allocation and XFree86.
The problem I had (XFree86 was considering a disabled ethernet ROM
as active) was fixed by patching XFree86, but I'm not sure this is
the same problem...

Post your log and let's see...

--Jay++

